       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       Starting  with Netpbm 10.86 (March 2019), ppppmmbbrriigghhtteenn is obsolete.  Use
       ppaammbbrriigghhtteenn(1) instead.

       ppaammbbrriigghhtteenn is mostly backward compatible with  ppppmmbbrriigghhtteenn.   You  can
       use  the  ppaammbbrriigghhtteenn manual for ppppmmbbrriigghhtteenn as long as you ignore fea‐
       tures that were added after Netpbm 10.86.

       One way in which ppaammbbrriigghhtteenn is not backward compatible is that
         ppaammbbrriigghhtteenn does not have a --nnoorrmmaalliizzee option.  If you want
         that function, use ppnnmmnnoorrmm on the image before passing it to
         ppaammbbrriigghhtteenn.

       Another backward incompatibility is that ppaammbbrriigghhtteenn produces the
         same kind of output as the input, whereas ppppmmbbrriigghhtteenn always
         produces PPM.  If you need PPM output, pass the results through
         ppppmmttooppppmm.

       ppppmmbbrriigghhtteenn is currently implemented as a triviel program that
         invokes ppaammbbrriigghhtteenn, ppnnmmnnoorrmm, and ppppmmttooppppmm.


